WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.125
Chapter 2: Add Item. The full form for one item: photos, name, category, costs
and value. You need: one item, or a photo of it, and about 8 minutes. Required:
Item name. Everything else is optional. Cost and value are separate. Empty means
unknown. 0 means zero.

00:00:23.125 --> 00:00:33.125
Step 1. Open Add Item. On Home or in your Vault, press ADD ITEM (top right of
the card).

00:00:33.125 --> 00:00:48.000
Step 2. The Add Item form. Photo on the left. Details on the right in five
numbered sections. Only Item name has a star: it is the only required field.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Required and optional: What the form needs. Required: Item name (marked with a
star). Optional: photos, brand, set or series, certification, grade, condition,
notes. Optional: Universe, Category and Subcategory; location; purchase price;
current value. Extra costs (Tax, Shipping, Fees) are added after saving, on the
item page. Saving with no name does nothing. The cursor returns to Item name.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:29.250
Step 3. Save needs an Item name. If you press Save to Vault with no name,
nothing is saved and the cursor jumps back to Item name. Type a name and try
again.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:41.875
Step 4. Take a photo. Take photo opens the camera. Line the item up inside the
corner brackets and press the round button. (Simulated: The viewfinder shows a
test camera playing a synthetic, fictional toy picture. The browser's own camera
permission prompt cannot be captured.)

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:58.125
Step 5. Keep the photo or retake it. Save keeps the photo. Retake throws it away
and returns to the camera. Fine Tune lets you adjust it first. Drag the corners
to crop. (Simulated: Test camera picture.)

00:01:58.125 --> 00:02:15.625
Step 6. The photo is on your item. The photo appears as the Cover. Retake
replaces it. Identify with AI is optional and depends on your account. Typing
the details yourself always works.

00:02:15.625 --> 00:02:30.000
Step 7. Name it (required) and add what you know. Type the Item name. Brand and
Set / Series are optional but make the item easier to find later.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:52.875
Step 8. Choose Universe, Category and Subcategory. Open section 2, Category.
Pick a Universe first (here Pop Culture), then the Category (Toys & Figures)
and, if one fits, a Subcategory. They are optional, and each list narrows to
match the one before it.

00:02:52.875 --> 00:03:11.875
Step 9. Purchase price is separate from value. Purchase price is what you paid.
Current value is what you think it is worth now. Leave either one empty if you
do not know it: empty means unknown, not zero.

00:03:11.875 --> 00:03:37.875
Cost and value: Blank, zero and valuation. Blank = unknown. The item has no cost
or value on record. 0 = zero. A gift, or a value you decided is nothing. An item
with a purchase price but no valuation counts at its purchase price in your
Vault total. The Vault says so. No value is invented or stored. Add a valuation
whenever you know one. It replaces the stand-in.

00:03:37.875 --> 00:03:59.125
Step 10. Saved: you land in your Vault. A short message confirms the save and
you are taken to your Vault. Total value shows $38: the item has no valuation,
so it counts at what you paid, and the card says so (1 of 1 at purchase cost).

00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:09.375
Step 11. Open it and check. Open the item. The photo and the details you typed
are all there.

00:04:09.375 --> 00:04:27.125
Step 12. Purchase details live on the item. Extra costs are not on the Add Item
form. Open the item and press the pencil on the Purchase panel (Edit purchase)
to add Tax, Shipping and Fees.

00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:45.000
Step 13. Add the extra costs. Purchase price is already filled in. Add Tax and
Shipping. For Fees we typed 0 on purpose: there were none. 0 is a real answer,
while an empty box means unknown.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:05:10.500
Step 14. Extra costs saved. Press the check mark to save. Tax, Shipping and Fees
are listed separately from the purchase price. Fees shows $0, which is different
from the dashes left on Source and Order #. This panel rounds to whole dollars
(Tax 3.50 reads $4); the exact amounts are stored.

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:27.625
Step 15. Cost and value stay separate. The cost basis adds the extras exactly:
38.00 + 3.50 + 4.25 + 0 = $45.75. The item still has no valuation: nothing was
invented for the value.

00:05:27.625 --> 00:05:41.625
Step 16. Reload and check it stuck. Reload the page, or come back tomorrow: the
photo, name, category and costs are exactly as you left them.

00:05:41.625 --> 00:06:03.000
Step 17. Or upload a photo you already have. Upload opens your device's file
picker (your photo library on a phone). The photo goes straight on as the Cover,
with no crop step. Retake replaces it; the small x on the thumbnail removes it.
(Simulated: The uploaded file is a synthetic, fictional comic cover.)

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:22.500
Step 18. The form remembers your last category. Heads up: the form keeps the
Universe and Category from your last item to save you time. Change them whenever
the new item is different, as we did here for a comic.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:38.750
Step 19. A gift: type 0, not nothing. If an item cost you nothing, such as a
gift, type 0 in Purchase price. Leaving the box empty would mean you do not know
what it cost.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:55.500
Step 20. Zero stays zero, blank stays unknown. On the gift item, Purchase price
shows $0 (you said it was free). The other costs stay as dashes, because they
were never entered.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:21.500
Phone differences: Add Item on a phone. Same form, one column: photo first, then
the five sections. Take photo opens the in-app camera. Take Real Photo opens
your phone's camera app. Upload picks from your photo library. In our phone-size
test the round camera button sits partly behind the tab bar. Tap its visible top
edge, or use Upload or Take Real Photo. Scroll the form to reach the later
sections.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:38.375
Step 21. The Add Item form on a phone. On a phone the photo area comes first,
and the five numbered sections follow below it. Scroll down for the rest. Only
Item name is required.

00:07:38.375 --> 00:08:04.250
Step 22. Take a photo. Take photo opens the camera and the round button
captures. In this phone-size test the button sits partly behind the tab bar (see
the highlight): tap its top edge. Take Real Photo opens your phone's own camera
app instead, and Upload lets you pick a photo you already have. (Simulated: The
viewfinder shows a test camera playing a synthetic, fictional picture. On a real
phone the browser asks to allow the camera first; that prompt cannot be
captured.)

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:14.750
Step 23. Keep or retake. Tap Save to keep the photo, or Retake to throw it away
and shoot again. (Simulated: Test camera picture.)

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:28.625
Step 24. Type the name. Type the Item name. On a phone, the keyboard covers the
lower half, so scroll the form to reach the other sections.

00:08:28.625 --> 00:08:44.750
Step 25. Purchase price and current value. Open section 4, Value. Purchase price
is what you paid. Current value stays empty if you do not know it: empty means
unknown.

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:53.875
Step 26. Saved. Saving takes you to your Vault, where the new item is listed.

00:08:53.875 --> 00:09:19.875
Chapter 2 recap: You added an item properly. ADD ITEM opens the form. Only Item
name is required. Photos: take, keep or retake; or upload. Category is optional
and the form remembers your last one. Purchase price and value are separate;
blank is unknown, 0 is zero. Tax, Shipping and Fees are added on the item page.
Reload the item: everything persists.
